 17592186045417 true] [17592186432781 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432740 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432781 1079 #uuid "cd4c20e9-b428-5717-aa65-b028512ceffa" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432704 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432712 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432715 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432722 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432782 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432742 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432782 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432782 1077 "selection" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432782 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432742 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432782 1079 #uuid "d41a4fb2-3b50-5439-ab7b-d9726d39fc08" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432783 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432771 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432783 1069 "q-85420" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432783 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432783 1071 "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $35\\,284\\,43◻$ divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $2$\n\nII. $5$\n\nIII. $4$" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432783 1072 #uuid "072352b0-88b5-50de-9e91-38bf12444d03" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432783 1074 "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$ Remember that to determine whether a number is divisible by $3,$ we check whether the sum of the digits is divisible by $3.$\n\nFor the given number, the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n3+5+2+8+4+4+3+◻=29+◻.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits we can substitute into the blank.\n\n- If we substitute $2$ into the blank, we get $35\\,284\\,432,$ which is divisible by $2.$ However, it is not divisible by $3$ because the sum of the digits is $29+2=31,$ which is not divisible by $3.$ So, the number is *not* divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- If we substitute $5$ into the blank, we get $35\\,284\\,435,$ which is not divisible by $2.$ Therefore, it is not divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- If we substitute $4$ into the blank, we get $35\\,284\\,434,$ which is divisible by $2.$ The sum of the digits is $29+4=33,$ which is divisible by $3,$ so the number is also divisible by $3.$ Therefore, the number is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432784 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432772 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432784 1069 "q-223458" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432784 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432784 1071 "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $276$\n\nII. $647$\n\nIII. $805$" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432784 1072 #uuid "1d92850b-bd66-52a9-a628-fb23ae6c0162" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432784 1074 "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $276,$ we have that \n\n$$\n27-2(6)=27-12=15\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $276$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $647,$ we have that \n\n$$\n64-2(7)=64-14=50\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $647$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $805,$ we have that \n\n$$\n80-2(5)=80-10=70\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $805$ is divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432785 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432770 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432785 1069 "q-132405" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432785 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432785 1071 "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $185\\,346$\n\nII. $2\\,525\\,934$\n\nIII. $15\\,070\\,962$" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432785 1072 #uuid "245a9f1f-3fc0-594c-a273-205b94f4bf02" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432785 1074 "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $185\\,346$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+8+5+3+4+6=27\n$$\n\nSo, $185\\,346$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $2\\,525\\,934$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n2+5+2+5+9+3+4=30\n$$\n\nSo, $2\\,525\\,934$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $15\\,070\\,962$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+5+0+7+0+9+6+2=30\n$$\n\nSo, $15\\,070\\,962$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432786 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432775 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432786 1069 "q-85424" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432786 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432786 1071 "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $591\\,030\\,47◻$ divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $2$\n\nII. $5$\n\nIII. $4$" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432786 1072 #uuid "66ca27c6-8cac-5ac3-b80e-6fd1dcb7b6a5" 13194139534687 17592186045417 true] [17592186432786 1074 "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$ Remember that to determine whether a number is divisible by $3,$ we check whether the sum of the digits is divisible by $3.$\n\nFor the given number, the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n5+9+1+0+3+0+4+7+◻=29+◻.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits we can substitute into the blank.\n\n- If we substitute $2$ into the blank